  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trade mission agri-business to Bangladesh (CTM23BD01)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of this trade mission is to strengthen the relationship between Bangladesh and The Netherlands and enhance private sector and economic cooperation in the field of agriculture:&#x2022;	seeds and horticulture, including arable and protected horticulture, potato and floriculture; and&#x2022;	dairy. Through the mission the following goals can be achieved within these priority sub-sectors:1.	Business-to-Business (B2B) cooperation between Dutch and Bangladeshi SMEs is stimulated by networking and matchmaking;2.	Focus is on trade and investments that benefit people, create jobs and preferably, are accompanied by the transfer of knowledge and skills;3.	Through business cooperation, the aim is to enhance food and nutritional security in Bangladesh by ensuring the consistent supply of quality agricultural inputs including resilient varieties, promoting sustainable production technologies and appropriate mechanisation and storage.</narrative>
  </description>
